---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_21",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 21,
  "text": "<p> [[62.1]] <b>19. LEIBNIZ AN LAMBERT VAN VELTHUYSEN</p>\n<p> [[62.2]] Frankfurt, 6./16. April 1670. [21.]</b></p>\n<p> [[62.20]] Nobilissime atque Amplissime Domine. </p>\n<p> [[62.21]] Miraberis literas ab ignoto, sed non et affectum; credo enim quod ego de me profiteor,\n[[62.22]] idem et alios dicturos, se cum primum libros tuos inspicere datum est, protinus Tui admiratione\n[[62.23]] captos esse. Vidi a Te, ita enim ajunt, <i>Dissertationem de principiis justi et decori Epistolicam</i>,\n[[62.24]] vidi <i>specimen Crellianarum objectionum in satisfactionem Christi refutatarum auctore L.V.</i> id\n[[62.25]] est Te. Vidi <i>initia primae philosophiae</i>, sed et quae <i>de generatione ac Liene</i> scripsisti ac\n[[62.26]] praefatus es. Reliquorum nihil hactenus in manus meas pervenit, sed quae tamen ex visis\n[[62.27]] aestimem. Nolo apud te tua laudando adulatoris suspicionem incurrere: illud dicere necesse est,\n[[63.1]] inter paucos saeculi nostri te numerandum qui contra torrentem plebeïum generoso nisu surrexerunt.\n[[63.2]] Procul illi sunto, qui mutata senectute pro Aristotele nobis Cartesium substituunt, qui\n[[63.3]] Gassendum, qui Hobbium, qui omnium unum, ut numen venerantur. Utinam vero meditationes\n[[63.4]] publico ne invideas, quas haud dubie multas et magnas alias animo concepisti, saltem ut\n[[63.5]] habeamus systema philosophematum tuorum, multo solidiore scientia nos beaturum, quam si\n[[63.6]] pro parte tantum nobis felicibus esse liceat. Scintilla illa lucis, quam in re medica dedisti,\n[[63.7]] utinam in flammam emicet. Tu inter paucos es, qui ei scientiae artem demonstrandi attuleris.\n[[63.8]] Non potes genus humanum melius demereri, quam si institutiones medicas ex tuis hypothesibus\n[[63.9]] conscribas. Et vero nosti ipse ac demonstrasti, id maxime Deo gratum esse, quod publice\n[[63.10]] utilissimum. Sed nec animae medicinam omittes, in qua facienda satis constat, quanto [apparatu]\n[[63.11]] officina tua instructa sit. </p>\n<p> [[63.12]] De jure naturali condi aliquando scientiam, omnium in universum interest, sed talem in\n[[63.13]] qua nihil addi nec claritati, nec veritati possit, <b>certum</b> enim definio, cujus veritas clara est.\n[[63.14]] Non ignoras quid Grotio, Hobbio, Sharrokio, Pallavicino, Ivoni [Parisino], Caramueli, Thomae\n[[63.15]] Anglo in <i>statera morum</i>, atque adeo ipsi Aristoteli desit. Cartesius haec raro attigit, et fere in\n[[63.16]] Epistolis tantum. Grotii summa eruditio, sed impar philosophia. Hobbius et intra generalia\n[[63.17]] nimium subsistit, et ea principia ponit institui, quae si sola sunt, licebit latere speranti quidvis\n[[63.18]] agere, tunc enim pax non violatur, ultimum juris apud Hobbium principium. Sed hoc non ideo\n[[63.19]] dico, ut virum incomparabilem sugillem, quem ego prope ante omnes nostri saeculi philosophos\n[[63.20]] admiror et colo, sed ut appareat, in negotio philosophiae moralis omnia fere de integro\n[[63.21]] resumenda esse. Expendi libellum <i>de Cive</i> diligenter, videoque esse alicubi hiatus catenae\n[[63.22]] demonstrationis. Ad has autem curas necessitate quadam deveni. Cum enim diu agitaverim\n[[63.23]] animo Rationalia Juris romani, multa versatione deprehendi, haec nisi scientia juris naturalis\n[[63.24]] instituta frustra quaeri. Quando exploratum est prope dimidiam partem Digestorum juris naturalis\n[[63.25]] esse, atque plerasque propositiones ab Jurisconsultis Romanis tanta subtilitate demonstratas,\n[[63.26]] ut cum Euclide certare possint, reliquae leges Juris romani, etsi non naturalis Juris,\n[[63.27]] tamen aliarum legum cum naturali jure combinatarum consequentiae haberi debent. Hoc igitur\n[[63.28]] ostenso, digestisque eo ordine legibus, quo se demonstrant aut consequuntur, eadem opera\n[[63.29]] Rationalia juris Romani, corpus juris reconcinnatum, jus romanum naturali collatum, ipsa\n[[63.30]] legum interpretatio ex ratione ea[ru]m velut animo pendens, denique scientia juris naturalis\n[[63.31]] accurate demonstrata habebuntur. Grotius Hobbiusque in multis solida juris naturalis stricti\n[[63.32]] principia aut subvertunt aut transiliunt, ut cum jus reale personali, contractus bonae fidei stricti\n[[63.33]] juris contractibus, pacta nuda conventionibus cum causa jure gentium aequipollere aut contendunt\n[[64.1]] aut innuunt. Utinam sententiam tuam discere liceat. Clarus Horbius spem mihi favoris tui\n[[64.2]] non exiguam fecit. Amplissimus Vir Er[icus] Mauritius literis Chilonio datis honorificentissime\n[[64.3]] de te judicavit, quae omnia mihi jam tum in notitiam tuam ardenti stimulos addiderunt. </p>\n<p> [[64.4]] Germania nostra viris quos tu aestimes non admodum multis instructa est. Joh. Lud.\n[[64.5]] Fabricius, Heidelbergus Theologus, ostendit erectioris se animi esse quam vulgo solent, certe\n[[64.6]] ejus Meditationes satis argumentum rei praebent. Joh. Joach. Becherus, medicus apud Electorem\n[[64.7]] Bavarum (nisi nuperrime mutaverit) vir est maximi ingenii, sed paulo inquietioris, quod\n[[64.8]] ei passim odia accersivit. Hermannus Conringius solidae utique doctrinae vir est, sed jam senio\n[[64.9]] gravatur. Paucissimos habemus a quibus aliquid magni sperandum videatur: Literatores multos,\n[[64.10]] philosophos aut paucos aut nullos. </p>\n<p> [[64.11]] De Tractatu Tuo <i>de Superstitione et idololatria</i> multa apud nos feruntur, ipsummet\n[[64.12]] nondum videre datum est. Utinam si rescribere dignaris, mentionem facere ne graveris eorum\n[[64.13]] virorum quos Tu in Belgio potissimum aut alibi ex solida philosophiae, naturalisque scientiae,\n[[64.14]] aut matheseos cognitione novisque cogitationibus maxime aestimes. Si quid vicissim mihi\n[[64.15]] imponis, nihil in me diligentiae desiderari patiar. Vale, volanti calamo ignosce, faveque </p>\n<p> [[64.16]] Vir amplissime Cultori Tuo Gottfredo Guilielmo Leibnitio. </p>\n<p> [[64.17]] Francof. 6/16 April. 1670. </p>\n<p> [[64.18]] P. S. Literae, si me responsione dignaris, dirigi possunt Moguntiam, operculo illis circumdato\n[[64.19]] ad Illustrissimum Bar. Boineburgium etc. maximis negotiis et incredibili eruditione\n[[64.20]] notissimum qui Te magni facit. </p>\n<p> [[64.21]] Nobilissimo et Amplissimo Viro Domino Lamberto Velthusio. Ultrajecti. </p>\n",
  "number": "19.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN LAMBERT VAN VELTHUYSEN",
  "date": "Frankfurt, 6./16. April 1670. [21.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:19. LEIBNIZ AN LAMBERT VAN VELTHUYSEN Frankfurt, 6./16. April 1670. [21.] Nobilissime atque Amplissime Domine. Miraberis literas ab ignoto, sed non et affectum; credo enim quod ego de me profiteor, idem et alios dicturos, se cum primum libros tuos inspicere datum est, protinus Tui admiratione captos...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>